    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `GET /api/owners/{id}` response is an `OwnerDto` generated from `openapi.yml` and populated by the MapStruct `OwnerMapper`. I added the derived field there, mirroring the existing `locality`/`membershipLevel` pattern:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema (so the DTO gains the field + setter on regeneration).\n\n2. **`ContactPreferences.java`** (new, in the `mapper` package) \u2014 a tiny cohesive helper mirroring `Localities`: `preferenceOf(owner)` returns `\"EMAIL\"` when `owner.getEmail() != null`, else `\"PHONE\"`. I used the same \"email present\" convention (`getEmail() != null`) that `MembershipLevels` already uses.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping(... expression = \"java(ContactPreferences.preferenceOf(owner))\")` line.\n\n## Structural impact\n\nThe behaviour lives in a brand-new class with zero surrounding methods (`WMC_other = 0`), so it contributes almost nothing to the cost. The only pre-existing method touched is the `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` interface declaration \u2014 a single added annotation line, CC 1. I deliberately avoided growing any existing method or touching the large controller class, and used a plain `string` (not an OpenAPI `enum`) to avoid a generated enum type and the type-conversion complexity that would come with it.",
